# Freenances Architecture

Personal + business finance app via Open Finance. Dual ledger (PF/PJ), money flows, narrative feed.

## Layer map

```
src/
├── domain/          Pure business rules (types, validators, pure functions)
├── application/     Use cases + ports (interfaces for external services)
├── infrastructure/  Adapters (Prisma, Better Auth, Pluggy)
├── ui/              Design tokens, primitives, patterns
└── app/             Next.js routes (pages, layouts, API handlers)
```

## Dependency direction

```
app → application, infrastructure, ui, domain
application → domain, application/ports
infrastructure → domain, application/ports
ui → domain (display types only)
domain → nothing external
```

Never import `infrastructure/` or `app/` from `domain/`. Never import Prisma or Next.js in `domain/`.

## Domain concepts

- **ContextType**: `PERSONAL` | `BUSINESS` — strict PF/PJ separation
- **Money flows**: OBLIGATIONS → RESERVES → DISCRETIONARY → INVESTMENT
- **Narrative feed**: human-readable `DomainEvent` items, not spreadsheet rows
- **Open Finance**: `IOpenFinanceProvider` port; Pluggy live or stub without credentials

## Conventions

- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`
- Branch: `feature/<kebab-case-english>`
- Commit: `tipo: mensagem em pt-BR` (feat, fix, chore, docs, test)
- README and file comments in English; UI copy may be English or pt-BR

## Next.js

Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing Next.js code — this project uses Next.js 16 with breaking changes from older versions.
